<task id="245b" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Run context, part 2 (G25) — values L2 owns: artifact versions computed from the artifacts used, SPE owner-certificate vault + secret name as validated options, H9 publishes the BFF URL + build id, H13/H14 read them</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T245 (G25, notes/run-context-dataflow-gap.md)</phase>
    <gate>none (T245a ✅)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies production .cs (H0 probe, H2a, H2b, H4, H4b, H8, H9, H13, H14, T6 probe, options, DAG) and their tests; root §8 test-modifying override applies.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting change to idempotency keys of four handlers plus options + DAG; idempotency-key changes affect resume semantics (high blast radius).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>shares HandlerRunInputs / RunContextContractTests / InterStepState / DagAdvancer with T245a, T245c, T238 (sequential by design)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>245a</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, l2-controlplane, provisioning-handler, config, testing, customer-provisioning</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Close the T245a known gaps owned by L2 itself: compute `bicepVer`, `indexVer` and `secretsVer` from the artifact each
    handler actually uses instead of requiring them as run parameters; make the SPE owner-certificate vault and secret
    name one validated L2 option used by H0, H8 and the T6 probe; have H9 write the BFF URL and deployed build id to
    `InterStepState` for H13 and H14; move H13's registry URL and scripts directory to options.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer on the L2 provisioning control plane. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in C#/.NET 10
    options validation (ValidateOnStart), content hashing, and idempotent handler design.
  </role>

  <goal>
    After this task: (1) no run parameter named `bicepVer`, `indexVer` or `secretsVer` is read — each handler derives its
    idempotency version from the content of the artifact it deploys/applies (same artifact ⇒ same version); (2) H0's
    certificate probe, H8 and the T6 probe read the SPE owner-certificate vault + secret name from one options type
    validated at Worker startup, and the H0/H8 secret-name mismatch (`spe-owner-cert-pfx` vs `SPE-OwnerCert-Pfx`) is
    resolved to the name that exists; (3) H9 writes `BffApiUrl` and `BffBuildId` to `InterStepState` and H13/H14 read
    them, with H14 ← H9 in the DAG; (4) every T245b known gap in `RunContextContractTests` is gone.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Evidence: notes/run-context-dataflow-gap.md. The three versions are idempotency-key components documented as
      content hashes (H2a: git SHA of infrastructure/bicep, `H2a:74-80,270-276`; H2b: hash of the schema JSONs in
      scripts/ai-search, `H2b:89-90,246-250`; H4/H4b: manifest content hash, `H4:84-85,163`) but computed nowhere. H12a
      already hashes its own manifest (`FileSeedManifestReader.cs:65`) — the reference implementation. The H0 probe
      targets the Spaarke platform vault (`KeyVaultCertBootstrapProbe.cs:30-33,55,92`) via run parameter `keyVaultName`;
      H8 reads `keyVaultName` + optional `speCertSecretName` (`H8:112-115`, default `SpeContainerOptions.DefaultCertSecretName`
      = `SPE-OwnerCert-Pfx`); the H0 probe checks `spe-owner-cert-pfx` — Key Vault names ignore case but not hyphens, so
      these are different secrets. H13 requires `buildId` + `bffApiUrl` (`H13:133-136,255-261`); H9 resolves the build
      from `latest.json` when `buildId` is absent (`H9:191-199`); H14 requires `webhookNotificationBaseUrl` = the BFF base
      URL (`H14:107`). H13 ← H14 ← H12c and nothing depends on H9 (`DagAdvancer.cs:140-163`), so today H13/H14 can run
      before the BFF is deployed.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BicepInfraDeploy/{H2aBicepInfraDeployHandler,ArmDeploymentRunner}.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/AiSearchIndex/H2bAiSearchIndexHandler.cs</file>
