    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project — idempotency semantics (BINDING)">
      Each computed version is a deterministic hash of the exact bytes the handler deploys/applies in this run (template
      JSON for H2a, the index schema set for H2b, the embedded manifest for H4/H4b). The idempotency-key format strings
      (`infra-…`, `aisearch-…`, `kv-…`, `appsettings-…`) stay unchanged. A run resumed with the same artifacts produces
      the same key.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / KV credential lifecycle (BINDING)">
      Read-only checks only against live Key Vaults (secret-name existence via the operator's own identity, NFR-11). No
      secret is created, renamed, copied or deleted. Never touch `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (either casing),
      `Dataverse-ClientSecret`, the soft-deleted rollback copies, or E-1 secrets.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010 / config constraints">
      The SPE owner-certificate setting extends the existing `SpeContainerOptions` (no new options type unless H0's
      options cannot reference it); required values validate at startup (ValidateOnStart), not at first use.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="project — scope">
      No change to `Sprk.Bff.Api`. T245c scope (H11 users, H14 Exchange group + Graph resources) is out of scope.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/run-context-dataflow-gap.md</file>
