      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/AiSeedChain/FileSeedManifestReader.cs (hash reference)</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">For H2a, H2b, H4, H4b: locate the artifact each one uses (template source, schema files, embedded manifest) and replace the `bicepVer`/`indexVer`/`secretsVer` parameter read with a hash of those bytes (shared helper if two handlers hash the same artifact). Keep rejection codes for "artifact unreadable".</step>
    <step order="2">Find which SPE owner-certificate secret name exists in the platform vault(s) the probes target (read-only `az keyvault secret list --query [].name` under the operator identity) and record it; make `SpeContainerOptions` carry the vault name + secret name (validated at startup); H0's probe, H8 and the T6 probe read them; drop the `keyVaultName` / `speCertSecretName` run parameters for this purpose.</step>
    <step order="3">H9: write `InterStepState.BffApiUrl` (production slot URL of the deployed App Service) and `InterStepState.BffBuildId` (the build it deployed) with `[ProducedBy(H9)]`; H13 reads both from InterStepState; H14 reads `BffApiUrl` for its webhook base URL. DAG: H14 ← {H12c, H9}.</step>
    <step order="4">H13 `registryDataverseUrl` / `provisioningScriptsDirectory` → `H13AcceptanceOptions` (validated, with the current defaults).</step>
    <step order="4b">Secrets-channel gaps pinned by T245a (`RunContextContractTests.PinnedManifestGaps`): (a) the Spaarke-shared vendor keys `BingSearch-ApiKey`, `ContentSafety-ApiKey`, `LlamaParse-ApiKey` (owner D5) — their source is a Spaarke platform-vault secret: make it validated L2 configuration (canonical name → platform vault + secret) that H4 copies from, replacing the `run.Parameters.Secrets` reference nothing writes; (b) `Dataverse-ServiceUrl` is H5's `InterStepState.DataverseEnvUrl`, and H5 is not a DAG ancestor of H4 — choose between H4 ← H5 and moving the value to an H4b `per_env_settings` entry (`from-h5-output`, with H4b ← H5), per the escalation trigger. Remove the fixed entries from `PinnedManifestGaps`. Since T245a, `TrapVerificationRequest.SpeOwnerCertKeyVaultName` (T6) is filled from the interim intake `keyVaultName` — point it at the new SPE owner-certificate option.</step>
    <step order="4c">Gaps added by the T245a quality gates (2026-10-01): (a) H7 `bffApiBaseUrl` — the stamp's own BFF URL is the same H9 output as step 3; today H7 falls back to the PLATFORM BFF `https://api.spaarke.com`, which is wrong for a dedicated stamp — read `InterStepState.BffApiUrl` and remove the default (DAG: H7 needs an H9 ancestor — decide H7 ← H9 vs a later env-var write, per the escalation trigger); (b) H13 registry columns `bffVersion` (H9 output — the deployed build), `solutionVersion` (H6 output — derive from `InterStepState.ImportedSolutions`) and `clientCacheBustToken` (mint per deploy/upgrade — decide which handler owns it); (c) 🔒 H4's KV RBAC bootstrap grants Key Vault Secrets Officer to `InterStepState.MiObjectId` — the customer stamp's BFF UAMI — when the identity that writes the secrets is L2's own (the bootstrapper's intent, `ArmOperatorKvRbacBootstrapper.cs` header). Make L2's principal object id validated L2 configuration (as `cosmos-provisioning.bicep` already takes `controlPlanePrincipalId`), grant THAT principal, and stop granting the stamp UAMI write access (Bicep already gives it Secrets User). Security-sensitive — **owner APPROVED this fix 2026-10-01** ("yes follow recommendation"): grant L2's configured principal, stop granting the stamp UAMI.</step>
    <step order="5">Remove the T245b entries from the pinned known-gap list; declare the new inputs in HandlerRunInputs; run RunContextContractTests.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests, build, docs (constraints/pattern pointer if the contract wording changes, design.md §6.2 keys, gap note §5), TASK-INDEX `✅ [done]`, POML status.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If neither SPE owner-certificate secret name exists in the platform vault, or both exist with different values, STOP and escalate (do not create or copy a secret).</trigger>
    <trigger>If H2a's template source is not a single deterministic artifact (e.g. chosen per run by an operator), STOP and escalate — the version may be a release-selection decision, not a hash.</trigger>
    <trigger>Dataverse-ServiceUrl: if neither H4 ← H5 nor an H4b per_env_settings entry is clearly better (H4 ← H5 delays the KV/app-reg chain behind Dataverse environment creation; the per_env route turns a KV reference into a literal app setting), STOP and present both to the owner.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>H12a's FileSeedManifestReader already hashes its manifest (FileSeedManifestReader.cs:65); SpeContainerOptions exists (SpeContainerOptions.cs:24); H13AcceptanceOptions exists.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extend SpeContainerOptions and H13AcceptanceOptions and add two InterStepState properties; the only possible new code is a shared content-hash helper if two handlers hash the same artifact.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Every run fails at H0 (cert vault), H2a (bicepVer), H2b (indexVer), H4/H4b (secretsVer) and H13 (buildId/bffApiUrl); H13/H14 can run before the BFF exists; H0 checks a different certificate secret than H8 uses.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">modified handler / options / DAG files listed above</output>
    <output type="test">updated tests for each modified handler + RunContextContractTests known-gap list</output>
    <output type="docs">notes/run-context-dataflow-gap.md §5, design.md §6.2</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">H2a, H2b, H4 and H4b succeed with no bicepVer/indexVer/secretsVer run parameter; the same artifact bytes give the same idempotency key across two runs; changed bytes give a different key.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Worker fails startup when the SPE owner-certificate vault or secret name option is blank; H0's probe and H8 use the same configured secret name; the H0/H8 mismatch is gone.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">After H9 succeeds, InterStepState has BffApiUrl and BffBuildId; H13 and H14 read them; H14 is not ready until H9 has completed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The pinned known-gap list contains only T245c entries; `PinnedManifestGaps` contains only the T245c (`Communication-DefaultMailbox`) and T225b (`Dataverse-ClientSecret`, `BFF-API-ClientSecret`) entries; RunContextContractTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H4 writes the three vendor keys into the customer vault from the configured platform-vault source with no `run.Parameters.Secrets` reference, and `Dataverse-ServiceUrl` reaches the BFF from H5's output; a missing vendor-key configuration fails Worker startup.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H7 writes `sprk_BffApiBaseUrl` from the stamp's own BFF URL with no `https://api.spaarke.com` fallback; H13 fills `sprk_bffversion`, `sprk_solutionversion` and `sprk_clientcachebusttoken` from handler outputs; H4's KV RBAC bootstrap grants the configured L2 principal (blank → Worker startup fails) and never the stamp UAMI.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build 0/0; no new ControlPlane.Tests failures beyond the T221 baseline; ArchTests pass. Test scope: the behaviours above (determinism + change detection per version, startup validation, H9 outputs + H14 readiness). Anything beyond needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    COMPLETION (2026-10-01). Verified: ControlPlane.Tests 2119 pass / 6 fail (the T221
    CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests baseline) / 1 skip; ArchTests 337/337; Api, Worker, LoadTests build 0/0;
    Invoke-CatalogGenerator.ps1 -Verify OK; customer.json + platform-controlplane.json recompiled (bicep 0.46.1);
    task-status drift check exit 0. Full account: notes/run-context-dataflow-gap.md §6.

    ESCALATION TRIGGER 1 FIRED (surfaced to the owner, nothing created or copied): no SPE owning-app certificate exists
    under either name in any Spaarke vault the operator identity can read (name-only check, NFR-11). The code does not
    depend on it existing — the credential is per-container-type configuration — but H0 rejects every run until the
    topology runbook creates the certificate (plan G28). Triggers 2 and 3 did not fire (H2a's template is the single
    CI-published artifact per tenancy model; the per_env route for Dataverse-ServiceUrl was better on all three counts).

    DEVIATIONS FROM THE CLOSED ACCEPTANCE SET (each surfaced to the owner):
    - AC-2: the owner credential is a LIST keyed by container type (SpeContainerOptions.ContainerTypeOwners), not one
      vault + secret-name option — an owning app is bound to one container type permanently (topology R1) and one L2
      provisions into several. An incomplete entry fails Worker startup; an EMPTY list boots and H0 rejects every run.
      Found on the way and fixed: H8 and T6 authenticated as the customer BFF app with the owner certificate, which
      could never succeed (the certificate is the owning app's; topology §3A).
    - AC-4 / AC-5: two vendor keys, not three. ContentSafety-ApiKey stays pinned under new task T246 (plan G26):
      stamps have no Content Safety resource and the BFF falls back to a dev endpoint. A missing vendor-vault NAME
      fails startup; a missing vendor SECRET fails H4 Resumable before any write (pre-resolution).
    - Dataverse-ServiceUrl moved to H4b per_env settings (Dataverse__ServiceUrl / Dataverse__EnvironmentUrl from
      from-h5-output:dataverse_env_url), H4b ← H5. Consequence: H9 (and H10–H14 behind it) now waits on H5.
    - registryDataverseUrl was DELETED, not moved to options — the registry updater never read it.
    - H13 registry columns (spec ADR-020 row PROPOSED): sprk_bffversion = H9's build id; sprk_solutionversion = a
      32-hex fingerprint of the imported solution set (no release-tag producer until T218); sprk_clientcachebusttoken
      = the run id.
    - ADR-028 E-1 scope (spec row PROPOSED, Path B recommended): L2 H0/H8/T6 use the owning-app certificate.

    FOUND AND FIXED BEYOND THE STEPS (fix-at-discovery): the H2a structural inspector could never run (it read
    infrastructure/bicep/ from a publish output that never contains it) and its per-customer-Redis rule contradicted
    D-12 — rebuilt as ArmTemplateInspector over the resolved ARM JSON, rule retired; H2a duplicate delivery of a
    completed step is a no-op that does not re-resolve the template; the A44.5 requireSecretFreeIdentity gate lost in
    master merge 92b480500 restored in the Worker Bicep; /provision-environment Step 6a used unassigned variables;
    customer.json and platform-controlplane.json were stale; publish-provisioning-arm-artifacts.yml did not trigger on
    scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/generated/** (customer.bicep composes kv-secrets.generated.bicep); live references
    to the deleted FileBicepTemplateInspector repointed at ArmDeploymentRunner.ResolveArmTemplateAsync.
    Considered and rejected: a Bicep user-defined type for speContainerTypeOwners — it switches the whole platform
    template to languageVersion 2.0 (symbolic resources) for a shape check SpeContainerOptions.Validate() already does.

    Test-scope justification (beyond the closed list): ArmTemplateInspectorTests (the inspector is new code with its
    own rules R2/R3); SpeContainerOptionsTests (topology-R1 validation rules + id canonicalisation);
    WorkerL2OwnedOptionsBootTests (the startup-failure ACs need the real composition root);
    SecretClientKvWriter pre-resolution test (a missing vendor secret must fail before any write).
  </notes>

